  "id": "free-will",
  "term": "free will",
  "definition": "In this historical Augustinian view, free will is the soul’s power to choose and the basis that makes moral life possible. It can also mean freedom for the good, but in that sense human freedom in ordinary life is held to depend on divine grace and to have been damaged by sin.",
